Main Dashboard:
- When the "Arrived Early" is filled, the stats on the statcards are not updated until you update the page.
- On the hour goal-statcard, when hovering over the grey portion of the progress bar, it should show the hour deficit(if any), ie how far you are from the goal.
- On the hour goal-statcard, make the progress bar about 20% thicker.
- The message "2 shifts in February belong to March payroll (19,70h)" is nice, but maybe you can click to expand, so it shows the shifts/dates and the hours?

All Calendars:
- Change to list view where each shift is a row in a list/table
- If i change my hourly/monthly rate, it changes the pay amount backwards. Like with the tax profiles, it should only count from now and forward. -- maybe lock the input field and make a change base pay menu? not sure what is smarter. You should be able to set the date, it shouldnt just use todays date.

Workplace dashboard:
- Add a button that includes planned shifts in the stats etc.
- The month picker should be at the top, just under the workplace name.
- Edit Workplace, Customize Appearance, Delete, and Payslip editor should be moved to a hamburger menu that is located where the delete button is (top/left in the same level as the company name/logo)
- Back-button: if you change the month, the back button should not go back to the month you were on before, it should go back to the main dashboard or workplaces overview.
- The tables are a bit cluttered. Their position should automatically changed according to what is configured for the workplace. They should go from top/left to bottom/right in the following order:
1. Details
2. Feriepenge / Flexkonto
3. Pension
4. Fritvalgskonto
- In the details table, it should calculate base / effective / total hourly wage for salaried positions
- In the details table, please put a hr below the wages and the weekly hours

Payslip Editor
- Buttons to change month
- Add the net hourly wage (net pay / total hours)
- Net pay is always in the bottom and gross pay is always in the top
- Custom lines default placement: Deductions are placed after subtotal(after tax), additions are placed just under gross pay
- Automatic recalculation after each change (when creating/removing or moving a custom line.) -- remove the button.

- In the navbar, color the page you are currently on, to help with navigation / knowing where you are

Workplace calendar:
- Work shifts for days that are before the start or after the end of the payroll period should be greyed out on the calendar. -- just like on the planning calendar
- When clicking the calendar, currently it opens a modal, i would like this to appear as a pop-up just over the date you clicked (like the pick-workplace-popup on the planning calendar)
- If no work shifts are already on the current day, it should automatically open the dialogue to add a new shift
- There should be a date field, so you can change it if you click the wrong date
- At the top of the add work shift form, there should be a small banner showing which workplace you are adding a shift for.
- In the add work shift form, it should show the shift time in minutes and decimal with and without the break
- When you are done adding a work shift, you should be returned to the workplace dashboard, not the main dashboard.

- In the workplace settings, there should be a break policy configuration, where you can pick:
-- Break time is paid
-- Break time is static (ie you can only enter yes/no in the work shift configuration, and the break numbers are static)
-- Break time is variable and should be entered manually every time (like it is now)

