Analytics page:
- Average hours per month/week should be calculated (trailing over a configurable amount of months)
- Expected income for the entire year and each month.
- There should be an input for expected contract end for a workplace (optional). This should be taken into account in the expected pay calculations., ie if my contract ends in june, that workplace earns me nothing in july.

SU-page:
A page that lets me configure studieaktivitet for each month in the year, and then it calculates and shows the limit for how much I can earn, and then sums up all my earnings for month basis and the year. It should have a progression bar that shows how close I am to the limit. It should also show the expected earnings for the rest of the year based on my current average, and how that affects the limit.
- Then it should have a message like "You are trending to have an income of xx which is above the limit of yy for this year. Please work less." or "Everything looks good, you are trending to have an income of xx which is below the limit of yy for this year. Keep it up!" or "You are very close to the limit, you are trending to have an income of xx which is just below the limit of yy for this year. Be careful with how much you work the rest of the year!"
- It should also have a section that shows fast inkomst (salaried jobs) vs hourly income, and if close to or over the limit, it should suggest maximum weekly/monthly hours for hourly jobs to stay under the limit.
- Studieaktivitet is defined in three levels:
-- 1 (Aktiv og får SU)
-- 2 (SU fravalgt eller Orlov/Lønnet praktik/studieinaktiv)
-- 3 (Ikke er indskrevet, ikke flere SU klip)).
- The amounts for each level are changed every year and should thus be easily configurable like with ATP. The current rates are 1: 20.749 kr. per måned, 2: 23.598 kr. per måned, 3: 45.420 kr. per måned. If you have kids under 18, the yearly limit is increased by 34.129 kr. per child in 2026. -- so amount of children should also be configurable on the SU page. 